(Postmortem PM-2026-014: Delivery outage in prod-us2 on 12 March 2026) Tj T*
T*
(Status: Complete. Severity: SEV1. Incident commander: Priya Raman. Author: Tomas Lindqvist.) Tj T*
T*
(Summary) Tj T*
T*
(On 12 March 2026, webhook deliveries in the prod-us2 region stalled for 47 minutes, from 14:06) Tj T*
(to 14:53 UTC. Publishing kept working, so no events were lost, but 38% of deliveries in the) Tj T*
(region were delayed by more than ten minutes. Customers in prod-eu1 were not affected.) Tj T*
T*
(Impact) Tj T*
T*
(About 2,400 customers saw delayed deliveries. Four Enterprise customers opened support tickets.) Tj T*
(No data was lost and no event was delivered twice because of the incident. The Enterprise) Tj T*
(availability commitment covers the publishing API, which stayed up, so no service credits were) Tj T*
(owed.) Tj T*
T*
(Root cause) Tj T*
T*
(Version 3.5.0, deployed two days earlier, changed the retry scheduler to open a database) Tj T*
(transaction for every delivery it rescheduled and to keep it open while computing the backoff) Tj T*
(delay. Under normal load this was harmless. When a large customer endpoint started failing at) Tj T*
(14:02, the number of deliveries waiting for a retry grew quickly and every one of them held a) Tj T*
(connection.) Tj T*
T*
(The connection pool reached its limit, db.pool.max_connections = 200. Delivery workers share) Tj T*
(that pool, so they could no longer record delivery attempts. Instead of failing quickly they) Tj T*
(waited for a free connection, because db.pool.acquire_timeout_ms was set to 30000. Workers) Tj T*
(spent most of their time blocked, and the delivery queue backed up across all partitions.) Tj T*
ET
endstream
endobj
